COMPILER-43 instantiates the equality helper in the x86-64 emitter only, which is the whole of what root ruled (option A, 2026-09-01): the eq-helper machinery lives in codex/compiler/Emit/X86_64.codex and the cross lanes are plugs that receive IR and compare a constructor by pointer. Lowering now sends an instantiated generic recursive == to the emitter instead of the desugared __eq_<T>, so the cross plugs see a binary eq on a sum where they saw an apply; the answer they give is the same wrong one they gave before, because the shared helper they used compared the field at its bare type variable. DELETE THIS SIDECAR when the post-resolve specialization pass lands (registered as the follow-on to COMPILER-43), which is what makes the capability backend-independent. Not run cross while Renode is barred (root, 2026-09-01), so the cross behaviour here is UNMEASURED rather than known-red.
